From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] diskinfo, trim, recoverdisk: xnu's disk ioctls

FreeBSD's disk tools ask GEOM with the DIOCG* ioctls. xnu's disks answer
the DKIOC* ioctls of <sys/disk.h> (IOMediaBSDClient, and the md ramdisk
driver), so the calls go through compat/nd_disk.c: the media and sector
sizes from DKIOCGETBLOCKSIZE and DKIOCGETBLOCKCOUNT, the stripe size from
DKIOCGETPHYSICALBLOCKSIZE, DIOCGDELETE as DKIOCUNMAP, GEOM::candelete as
DKIOCGETFEATURES' DK_FEATURE_UNMAP, DIOCGFLUSH as DKIOCSYNCHRONIZE and
DIOCGPHYSPATH as DKIOCGETFIRMWAREPATH. The command lines are FreeBSD's.
GEOM's descr, ident, attachment, rotation rate and zone attributes and the
firmware geometry have no xnu counterpart: diskinfo -v leaves them out
(the rotation rate is Unknown), and diskinfo -s (the serial number) fails
with an error that says so. diskinfo -i and -S need aio_waitcomplete(2),
which xnu doesn't have, and fail the same way. recoverdisk already builds
without the ioctls; it now uses them.

